`Depends()` works great, but does not support post-response cleanup. How about injecting from context managers? Taking the [SQL Db example](https://fastapi.tiangolo.com/tutorial/sql-databases/), it would not need middleware anymore:



```python
from contextlib import contextmanager

@contextmanager
def db() -> Session:
    db_session = Session()
    try:
        yield db_session
    finally:
        db_session.close()

@app.get("/users/{user_id}")
def read_user(user_id: int, db_session: Session = Depends(db)):
    user = get_user(db_session, user_id=user_id)
    return user
```

